00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.980
If you’re finding me for the first time
be sure to subscribe to get that video.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.409
Time for some questions!

00:00:30.409 --> 00:00:34.680
Question Number 1 - Lily Love (no avatar)
asks This episode was a pretty faithful adaptation

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.010
from the comic book.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.570
What other storylines from the comic book
would you want to see be played out on the

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:39.570
show?

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.290
That’s easy, I think they should do the
Hunters this season.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:46.450
It was one of my predictions, but since they’re
not always 100% faithful to the comic they

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.380
might merge some characters together.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.940
There will be a new villain in the next couple
of episodes.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.260
Even if it’s a twist on the comic book story
I still hope they include some of the events

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.260
surrounding that group.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.500
Question Number 2 - Supercharged chargers
(no avatar) asks What do you think about only

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:04.260
seeing Rick, Michonne and Carl then the next
episode seeing only the other group?

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.260
﻿

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.870
I think it’s a good opportunity to spend
extra time on certain characters, it’s the

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:08.870
reason we got all that michonne and carl.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:12.830
The cast is so big it’s hard to give characters
a lot of scenes without taking potential scenes

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.080
away from others.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.159
So next week instead of Rick, Carl and Michonne.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:18.729
We’ll get Maggie, Glenn and everyone else.

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:20.930
Crossing my fingers on Baby Judith too.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:25.720
Question Number 3 - Andresm92 asks What was
that Michone's rampage?

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.380
The pain of what happened at the prison finally
got to her.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.930
So all the awful things from her past that
she shut out of her mind just got vomited

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.190
up in a hurricane of sword slashes.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:38.490
You could make the argument that just as carl
threw up after he escaped the pile of walkers.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.700
Michonne kind of vomited up all of the feels.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.960
Question Number 4 - Ben Roycroft asks Do you
feel that Rick will survive until the next

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.600
season or do you think he will meet his end
in the finale?

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:51.220
I think of the two big leaders right now,
Daryl and Rick, Rick will be the first one

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.220
to go.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.190
I know that someone is going to die before
the end of the season.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:57.530
But I think on the list of who it might be,
Rick is really low.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.560
So I do think he’ll make it to season 5.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.670
They’ve already deviated from the comic
in terms of characters that have died.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:08.009
Question Number 5 - Guijone Halili asks Do
you think baby Judith is alive?

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:09.590
Yes, I do.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.480
Mostly because what would be the reason to
not show her to us.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.340
It’s most likely that they want us to wonder
whether or not she’s dead.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:24.270
And by not having her in this episode it just
sweetens the payoff when we finally do 

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.270
find out.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:28.970
Question Number 6 - Monty Gonzales asks Did
Michonne know those footprints were Rick and

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.560
Carl as she followed them?

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.120
No, she just knew that they were the footprints
of people who survived.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.150
Walkers drag their feet, so that’s how she
knew they were alive.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.700
They were clean prints.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.050
She was probably just hoping they belonged
to friends.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.280
Question Number 7 - Zee Snake (no avatar)
asks Do you think Tara will become sort of

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.830
like Michonne after losing both her niece
and her girlfriend?

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.920
Do you think she'd withdraw from Lily as a
whole?

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.390
I’m actually really interested to see which
group they end up with.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.390
They’re both alive, but no.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.830
I think Lily is the one who will go nuts and
turn into someone like Michonne during season

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:56.830
3.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.830
Just completely numb.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.020
Tara was all talk, remember how she ended
up being a terrible shot when her girlfriend

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.800
was trying to practice with her.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.570
Question Number 8 - Josh Bello asks Do you
think Carol will show up by the end?

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.730
She’ll show up way before the end.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.250
Maybe not next week, but soon.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.760
I think she’ll run into Tyreese’s group
first and there will be this cloud of weirdness

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.230
hanging over them until tyreese finds out.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:21.130
I’m interested to see if he reacts the way
we expect him to, or if he surprises us and

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.430
just accepts it.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.160
Right now, my money is on him going crazy.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.040
Question Number 9 - Jarl Mikael asks Q&amp;A:
Why does Michonne's two zombies never try

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.010
to attack/bite her?

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.610
She tore off their jaws, so they can’t bite.

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:35.270
They’re literally just pets.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:38.940
They were actually two of the governors men.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.210
Question Number 10 - The Clay Sloth (no avatar)
asks Do you think they will introduce another

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:44.870
antagonist like the governor?﻿

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.690
Yes, everyone is wondering if it’s going
to be Negan, but that seems too far ahead.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:53.670
I think it will be the gareth character that
they cast.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:57.849
He’s new this season, but I think he’ll
be an amalgam of the leader of the hunters

00:03:57.849 --> 00:03:58.849
and negan.

00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:02.250
Or at least a minor villain if he doesn’t
last to season 5.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:06.810
and one more Bonus Question - Kevin Antihero
(no avatar) asks Will they will start following

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.370
the comic more closely?

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:12.360
Do you think the remaining survivors will
now head to Washington, D.C.?﻿

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.800
Just because they did in this episode, no.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.160
It will be like before, they’ll loosely
follow the plot of the comics.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:23.630
Yes I do think at least one group will make
it to washington DC.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.160
Or at least find out about it.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:29.780
The name of the finale is “A”, which everyone
is taking to mean Alexandria.

